# Deliberate design choice: raw/processed data and trained model binaries are
# NOT committed to git. Both are large/binary artifacts that don't diff
# meaningfully in git, and both are fully, deterministically regenerable
# (fixed RANDOM_SEED end-to-end) via the pipeline scripts. Lineage and
# integrity are tracked instead via content-hash manifests that ARE
# committed: data/DATA_VERSIONS.json and models/MODEL_VERSIONS.json.
# Regenerate everything with: see README "Reproduce from scratch".
data/raw/*.csv
data/processed/*.csv
models/*.joblib
logs/*.jsonl

# Same reasoning for Week 4 monitoring: the drifted input batch is
# regenerable (simulate_drift.py, fixed DRIFT_SEED). The monitoring log
# (predictions_vs_actuals.jsonl), report, retrain decision, and plot ARE
# committed below -- they're the actual Week 4 deliverable evidence.
monitoring/drifted_batch_raw.csv
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db
*.backup
